## 15. FAST, MOBILE-FIRST PERFORMANCE — TARGET APPROXIMATELY 2 SECONDS

Speed is a major requirement.

Engineer the website to target approximately two seconds for the initial useful page experience on a reasonably fast mobile connection, where hosting, network conditions, and third-party services allow it.

Use measured performance results rather than guaranteeing a universal loading time.

Implement:

- Mobile-first responsive layouts.
- Modern AVIF or WebP images where supported.
- Correct image dimensions and responsive image sources.
- Compressed imagery and appropriately sized product thumbnails.
- Lazy loading for below-the-fold images.
- Prioritized loading for the main hero image.
- Minimal JavaScript and a small dependency footprint.
- Server rendering or static generation where appropriate.
- Code splitting and dynamic loading for heavy components.
- Lazy initialization of the 3D visualizer.
- Font optimization and a minimal number of font weights.
- Caching, CDN delivery, and compression through the selected hosting platform.
- No unnecessary autoplay videos or oversized animation libraries.
- No blocking third-party widgets unless they are essential.
- Efficient catalogue filtering and calculator updates.
- Proper cleanup of 3D resources.

Measure performance using Lighthouse or suitable browser performance tools. Aim for strong Core Web Vitals and a mobile Lighthouse performance score of 90 or better when feasible.

Report any performance bottlenecks honestly. Do not claim a two-second load time or a successful benchmark until it has actually been measured.

